      "problem": "Given that $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ what is $\\text{Var}[X]?$",
      "worked_solution": "If $X∼\\text{Exp}(\\lambda )$ is an exponential random variable, then\n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[X]=\\frac{1}{{\\lambda }^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, for our random variable $X∼\\text{Exp}(2),$ we have the following variance:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X] & =\\frac{1}{(2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\  & =0.25\\end{aligned}\n$$",
